      en: "Stara Planina (Balkan Mountains) is a mountain range on the border between Serbia and Bulgaria. It is known for its numerous waterfalls, including the 15-meter high Pilj-Vodopad and the 10-meter high Čungulj. The region is part of the Stara Planina Nature Park, established in 2009. The waterfalls are especially impressive in spring after snowmelt. The surrounding forests are home to brown bears, wolves, and lynxes. Stara Planina is an important area for biodiversity protection with over 2,000 plant species. Traditional villages like Dojkinci preserve local culture. The waterfalls are accessible via hiking trails and are popular destinations for nature photographers.",
